      "content": "thanks. i'll paste a few threads here. just look for anything that feels scripted or too formal for the person sending it. i'm noticing a lot of people using the word 'protocol' or 'standardization' in casual threads where it doesn't belong. it's like they're using code words to signal that i'm being watched.\n\nhere is the first one: \n\nfrom: mark s.\nsubject: re: q3 report projections\nhey, just following up on the files you sent. we need to ensure the data adheres to the new standardization protocols before the end of the day. please confirm receipt of the updated guidelines. thanks.\n\nit's weird because mark usually just says \"hey, did you get those files?\" or \"send them over when u can.\" he never uses words like 'adheres' or 'protocols' in a casual email. does that seem like a deviation to you?",
